{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/26804-does-anybody-know-where-to-find-source-material-and-inspiration-for-mummy-the-curse","id":26804,"title":"Does anybody know where to find source material and inspiration for Mummy the curse?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T16:29:43-08:00","id":26804,"title":"Does anybody know where to find source material and inspiration for Mummy the curse?","content":"Hi, i am a long time Storyteller in the NWOD, and recently i acquired Mummy, but i cant find about any inspirations or source material for searching, i love the other game lines, among all of them the core world of darkness, so the lack of this source material mentioned in the core book is very dissapointing for me, i believe there should be a webpage or blog with some info, but the link is dead. Also wanted to ask if the Mummy game itself is easy for crossovering with other game lines, lets say Mage or Vampire, and if there is any info for roleplaying the game without using the default lore as given in the book, i mean, in other lines , if you wanted to play a more classical monster or change the backgrounds, the book gave you info and advices for doing this, but again this i cant find in the book, so any advices or ideas will be welcome ( i want to start campaign with all players as humans, and dont want to be tied to the Mummy official lore, in case somebody find more about mummies). Thanks in advance for all ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1599-dosan","name":"Dosan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:16:21-08:00","id":26872,"title":"","content":"The book's largest inspiration was <i>The Mummy</i> (1932). That's primarily, from what I can tell, how the Descent concept came to be. The movie <i>Pumpkinhead</i> was also listed as a good source by one of the writers on a forum once. My campaign is largely based on what the Mummy's perspective was in The Mummy films, including monster mash-ups like Dracula meets the Mummy, or whatever.<br /> <br /> Which leads us to crossover. I find the core-book's lack of word count to easily be its worst feature. So the developer opted for saying about Mummies rather than taking up precious space on how Mummies interact with other monsters. I plan on my PC coming across a Promethean, Werewolves, and some Vampires but they're tweaked a little in my campaign's mythos so that Mummies are very much the stars of the show. But really, if you're a long time WoD GM then there's more than enough resources available to inspire crossover; you can do the same with Mummy, it's just that at some point you'll have to use your own imagination rather than reading about it in a book.<br /> <br /> There's lots to be said between a Vampire's fog of memory and a Mummy's Memory, Atlantis and the Nameless Empire, Osiran Prometheans and the Rite of Return, and an upcoming Hunter supplement provides a new compact and conspiracy geared towards Mummy hunting. And that's before kicking into gear the awesome power of your own imagination!<br /> <br /> Asking yourself what sort of changes you want to see in the background is the first step towards figuring out those changes. Is there something about the back story you're not particularly keen on? Once you have more of an idea then I'd love to help! As it is, though, I personally think that having a more concrete background in Mummy (which is still very, very vague right now) is a feature and not a bug. Mummies are based on Memory, which means they <i>actually remember things</i>, which means you need to have an idea of what those things are, which means you can't necessarily have a loose, mysterious mythical background like Mage, for example.<br /> <br /> Also, it's important to note that a <i>character's background</i> is actually kinda more important than the setting background. Even if one of your players gleams some mystical truth about Irem by reading the Storyteller's section, that's not as important, meaningful, or impactful as that player learning what horrible things their Mummy executed and forgot over thousands of years","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":".  added fifth paragraph 12-09-2013, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T06:02:00-08:00","id":27135,"title":"","content":"Kismet Rose posted some thing ago her fan site for all things Mummy the Curse called the Nameless Empire Facebook page, thread is here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1165-mummy-on-facebook\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...my-on-facebook</a><br /> <br /> The direct link to the Nameless Empire fan page is: <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire</a><br /> <br /> go check it out, it posts art, fan pics, fan materials and all things for the Mummy lover. It is a real work of love and Kismet Rose is always updating it daily. Please support it.<br /> <br /> Since OPP has still not given us the much promised 'Scroll of Ages' website, this is a good place to start as well as the Official Mummy the Curse Facebook page, which is always updated regularly (and frequented by CAS himself).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T07:44:50-08:00","id":27186,"title":"","content":"Thanks, hope they rise The Scroll of Ages from the tomb someday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> since it has so much potential, i already love the music playlist the devs did for all the lines of games, i know they will have interesting info in the scroll. For me, one source of inspiration, although is not about a Mummy, is the game Planescape: Torment, one game about an inmortal that forgot his previous incarnations, kind of a &quot;must play&quot; classic for all the rpg gamers. It touches subjects as: &quot;What can change the nature of a man&quot; and the price of inmortality, among others. Highly recommended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1599-dosan","name":"Dosan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T06:00:04-08:00","id":27922,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing Dosan, I have not checked out Planescape, sounds like its themes are similar to some of Mummy's. <br /> Has anyone considered using Call of Cthulhu as a source for stories? I know its set in the 1920s but its got that pulp era feel that seems to fit Mummy pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:45:35-08:00","id":28265,"title":"","content":"That would be especially appropriate for the Dark Era for Mummy, which i believe is in the late 1800's to the 1920s. This is also the era that the original Mummy movies were set in. In general cthulhu mythos, the elder gods, etc is how ive been keeping the Duat mythos in theme. Ive even used cthulhu himself as a refererernce for Sutek, and Nyarlthotep as reference for Anpu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.